1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,090
Imagine a donkey

2
00:00:01,090 --> 00:00:02,760
standing exactly halfway

3
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:05,250
between two identical bales of hay:

4
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:06,170
same size,

5
00:00:06,170 --> 00:00:08,270
same distance, same smell,

6
00:00:08,270 --> 00:00:10,950
completely equal in every way.

7
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:12,360
The donkey is hungry,

8
00:00:12,360 --> 00:00:15,420
but because both options are perfectly identical,

9
00:00:15,420 --> 00:00:16,850
it has no rational reason

10
00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:18,830
to choose one over the other.

11
00:00:18,830 --> 00:00:20,250
So it stands there,

12
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:21,570
unable to decide,

13
00:00:21,570 --> 00:00:22,620
and eventually

14
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:24,490
it starves to death.

15
00:00:24,490 --> 00:00:26,890
If two options are truly equal,

16
00:00:26,890 --> 00:00:27,740
what makes you choose

17
00:00:27,740 --> 00:00:29,330
one over the other?

18
00:00:29,330 --> 00:00:31,030
Pure reason cannot decide

19
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:32,760
between identical options,

20
00:00:32,760 --> 00:00:34,770
so either the choice is made by something

21
00:00:34,770 --> 00:00:35,930
other than reason,

22
00:00:35,930 --> 00:00:36,910
or the options

23
00:00:36,910 --> 00:00:38,150
were never truly equal

24
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:39,620
to begin with.

25
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:41,310
It shows up in real life:

26
00:00:41,310 --> 00:00:42,670
choosing between two jobs

27
00:00:42,670 --> 00:00:44,230
that seem equally good,

28
00:00:44,230 --> 00:00:45,390
two apartments,

29
00:00:45,390 --> 00:00:45,870
two people

30
00:00:45,870 --> 00:00:47,520
you have feelings for.

31
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:48,520
The more rationally

32
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:50,430
you approach an identical choice,

33
00:00:50,430 --> 00:00:52,800
the more paralyzed you become.

34
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:54,380
Philosophers use this paradox

35
00:00:54,380 --> 00:00:56,310
to argue about free will.

36
00:00:56,310 --> 00:00:57,910
If a perfectly rational agent

37
00:00:57,910 --> 00:00:59,970
cannot choose between equal options

38
00:00:59,970 --> 00:01:01,990
without some external nudge,

39
00:01:01,990 --> 00:01:03,690
what exactly is making the choice

40
00:01:03,690 --> 00:01:04,770
in humans?

41
00:01:04,770 --> 00:01:05,830
Is it reason?

42
00:01:05,830 --> 00:01:07,120
Is it desire?

43
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:08,600
Is it something beneath both

44
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:10,270
that we never fully control?

